patrone-gnome-taskbar (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Layouts, apart from themes (the new "layout" setting): Left, Centered,
    Split (Start on the left, the apps in the middle) and Top, along the
    top of the screen, with its menus and tooltips opening downward and the
    running indicators along the screen's edge.
  * The Start button's icon (the new "start-icon" setting): the Patrone P,
    a one-color P, an orb, a grid, three lines, a circle, a spark or a
    prompt. The one-color ones take the bar's text color.
  * Themes: Royal is the old Classic, its green Start button without the
    word "start"; Classic is plain and square, a solid light or dark bar;
    Modern has rounder buttons and no line along the bar.
  * "Taskbar settings" opens GNOME Settings' Patrone page, in Patrone's
    build of GNOME Settings, or else Patrone Settings.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0500

patrone-gnome-taskbar (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Drag to reorder the taskbar's buttons and Start's pinned apps. An app
    that's only running, or one dragged from Start (Pinned or All apps), is
    pinned to the taskbar where it's dropped. A gap on the taskbar, and a
    blue line in Start, shows where it will go.
  * Sizes: small (32 pixels), medium (42, as before) or large (52), with
    the icons to match: the new "size" setting, which Patrone Settings
    sets.
  * Themes, from Patrone Settings (org.patrone.desktop theme): Patrone (as
    before), Modern (the buttons centered), Classic (a blue bar, a green
    Start button that says "start", a lighter blue tray) and Studio
    (translucent, the buttons centered on a rounded shelf).
  * "Taskbar settings" on the taskbar's right-click menu, when Patrone
    Settings is installed.
  * The taskbar takes its new height when the size or theme changes: the
    height it was given before had stuck.
  * The screen-sharing pill's white icons and colors hold in the light
    style too (St let the light and dark sheets' rules beat common.css's).

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:30:00 -0500

patrone-gnome-taskbar (0.1.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Start menu, as on Windows 11: the account picture and name open a menu
    with who's signed in, Change account settings, Lock and Sign out; the
    power button opens Sleep, Shut down and Restart (where the system
    allows them), and Disconnect while the desktop is seen through Remote
    Desktop, which ends the connection and leaves the desktop running. These
    replace the row of power buttons.
  * The taskbar is a third larger: 42 pixels, with its icons, tray, clock
    and running-app lines to match.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:30:00 -0500

patrone-gnome-taskbar (0.1.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Hide GNOME's screen-sharing indicator in desktops with no screen of
    their own (Patrone's): there it's always on, for the very Remote Desktop
    connection the desktop is seen through, and any click on it, a
    right-click included, cut that connection. It showed as two unexplained
    icons in the tray.
  * Style the screen-sharing and screen-recording indicators for the tray
    (an orange or red pill with white icons), where they still show.
  * Keep the tray from ever expanding: GNOME's top bar buttons ask to.

